      "problem": "Simplify the statement $\\neg ( (P \\lor \\neg Q) \\land (Q \\lor \\neg P) )$ using De Morgan's laws.",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∧Q)≡¬P∨¬Q, \\\\ ¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∧¬Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬((P∨¬Q)∧(Q∨¬P)) & ≡¬(P∨¬Q)∨¬(Q∨¬P) \\\\  & ≡(¬P∧¬(¬Q))∨(¬Q∧¬(¬P)) \\\\  & ≡(¬P∧Q)∨(¬Q∧P)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
